<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" xmlns:zeebe="http://camunda.org/schema/zeebe/1.0" id="Defs_craft_graph" targetNamespace="http://graph-agent/bpmn">
  <bpmn:process id="craft_graph" name="Craft a graph extension" isExecutable="true">
    <bpmn:documentation>Turning a prompt into new graph.

The agent proposes a small list of operations (GraphOp[], src/agent/graph.ts) --
new elements, not a whole document -- which graph:lint merges into the current
graph before anything else runs. The merged graph is laid out and linted, a
human approves it, and only then is it spliced into the running session.
Because this is itself a BPMN process, the act of extending the agent is as
visible and as auditable as the work the extension goes on to do.

The splice must be additive with stable ids: bpmn-engine replays recovered child
state by element id, so a fragment that renames or removes a live element cannot
be recovered. graph:extend rejects those before they are applied. applyGraphOps
only ever adds elements (or re-points an *existing* sequence flow while keeping
its own id), so this holds by construction rather than needing the model to get
a verbatim echo right.</bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:extensionElements>
      <zeebe:userTaskForm id="craft_review_form">{
  "$schema": "https://unpkg.com/@bpmn-io/form-js@1/dist/assets/form-json-schema/schema.json",
  "components": [
    {
      "label": "Apply this extension?",
      "type": "radio",
      "key": "approval",
      "id": "approval",
      "values": [
        {
          "label": "Apply",
          "value": "apply"
        },
        {
          "label": "Reject",
          "value": "reject"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "Notes for the agent",
      "type": "textarea",
      "key": "notes",
      "id": "notes"
    }
  ],
  "type": "default",
  "id": "craft_review_form",
  "schemaVersion": 18
}</zeebe:userTaskForm>
    </bpmn:extensionElements>
    <bpmn:startEvent id="craft_start" name="Intent">
      <bpmn:outgoing>to_draft</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="to_draft" sourceRef="craft_start" targetRef="gw_draft_entry" />
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="gw_draft_entry" name="Enter draft">
      <bpmn:documentation>A plain merge, not a decision: whichever of a fresh start or a redraft
loop-back arrives runs straight through to draft_fragment. Explicit rather
than the two incoming flows bpmnlint's fake-join rule used to merely warn
about (now an error) -- a real BPMN join needs a gateway; a plain activity
with more than one incoming edge does not join at all, it just runs again
per arrival, which is exactly the behaviour this gateway keeps.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>to_draft</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>lint_retry</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>into_draft_fragment</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="into_draft_fragment" sourceRef="gw_draft_entry" targetRef="draft_fragment" />
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="draft_fragment" name="Draft BPMN fragment">
      <bpmn:documentation>Resets extend_status to null on every entry (a fresh craft_start, or a
lint_retry redraft) -- apply_extension is the only activity that ever sets
it, and only on a successful splice, so without this reset a caller that
routes on extend_status (session-craft.bpmn's gw_crafted, chiefly) would see
a stale "success" from an earlier lap's craft_graph invocation survive into
a lap that rejected or gave up on this one.

Also republishes agent:turn's own resolved "prompt" output back to the
"prompt" variable: a callActivity does not process its own zeebe:ioMapping
(only a harness-backed activity does, in this project's engine wrapper) and
does not inherit the caller's variables either, so pi_default_loop's own
llm_turn -- reached through session-craft.bpmn's run_default fallback, in a
*different* linked process than this one -- would otherwise see "prompt" as
never seeded at all on any lap after the first, calling Pi's continue()
over a transcript that still ends on this activity's own unanswered
assistant turn (real Haiku repro: "Cannot continue from message role:
assistant"). The output source is "=prompt", not a re-derived
intent-or-prompt expression, because resolveOutput's scope is only the
harness's own returned result fields, never other process variables --
agent:turn's harness now returns the input it actually resolved this turn
as its own "prompt" result field for exactly this reason. Session-
skeleton.bpmn never reads "prompt" again after its own first lap, so this
republish is an inert overwrite there.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <zeebe:taskDefinition type="agent:turn" />
        <zeebe:taskHeaders>
          <zeebe:header key="agent_role" value="graph_architect" />
        </zeebe:taskHeaders>
        <zeebe:ioMapping>
          <zeebe:input source="=if intent = null then prompt else intent" target="prompt" />
          <zeebe:input source="=lint_feedback" target="lint_feedback" />
          <zeebe:output source="=text" target="fragment" />
          <zeebe:output source="=null" target="extend_status" />
          <zeebe:output source="=prompt" target="prompt" />
        </zeebe:ioMapping>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>into_draft_fragment</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>to_lint</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="to_lint" sourceRef="draft_fragment" targetRef="lint_fragment" />
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="lint_fragment" name="Merge and lint">
      <bpmn:documentation>Runs before layout now (issue: graph_architect drafting-representation
blocker): draft_fragment's own "fragment" output is an ops list, not a
document, and graph:layout needs a real, complete BPMN document to lay out --
one only exists once graph:lint has merged the ops into the current graph
(applyGraphOps, src/agent/graph.ts). On success this republishes the merged
document back onto "fragment" for layout_fragment (and, eventually,
apply_extension) to read.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <zeebe:taskDefinition type="graph:lint" />
        <zeebe:ioMapping>
          <zeebe:input source="=fragment" target="fragment" />
          <zeebe:output source="=status" target="lint_status" />
          <zeebe:output source="=summary" target="lint_feedback" />
          <zeebe:output source="=attempt" target="lint_attempts" />
          <zeebe:output source="=fragment" target="fragment" />
        </zeebe:ioMapping>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>to_lint</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>to_layout</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="to_layout" sourceRef="lint_fragment" targetRef="layout_fragment" />
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="layout_fragment" name="Auto-layout">
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <zeebe:taskDefinition type="graph:layout" />
        <zeebe:ioMapping>
          <zeebe:input source="=fragment" target="fragment" />
          <zeebe:output source="=fragment" target="fragment" />
        </zeebe:ioMapping>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>to_layout</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>to_gw_lint</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="to_gw_lint" sourceRef="layout_fragment" targetRef="gw_lint" />
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="gw_lint" name="Fragment valid?" default="lint_retry">
      <bpmn:documentation>Flows are evaluated in order, and the default is taken only when none
matched: valid first, then out of attempts, then redraft.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>to_gw_lint</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>lint_ok</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>lint_exhausted</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>lint_retry</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="lint_ok" name="valid" sourceRef="gw_lint" targetRef="review_fragment">
      <bpmn:conditionExpression xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">=lint_status = "success"</bpmn:conditionExpression>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="lint_exhausted" name="give up" sourceRef="gw_lint" targetRef="gw_rejected_entry">
      <bpmn:conditionExpression xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">=lint_attempts != null and lint_attempts &gt;= 3</bpmn:conditionExpression>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="gw_rejected_entry" name="Rejected">
      <bpmn:documentation>A plain merge of the two ways a lap ends without a splice -- a human
rejecting it, or the redraft cap giving up -- onto one end event, the same
reasoning as gw_draft_entry above.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>rejected</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>lint_exhausted</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>into_craft_rejected</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="into_craft_rejected" sourceRef="gw_rejected_entry" targetRef="craft_rejected" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="lint_retry" name="redraft" sourceRef="gw_lint" targetRef="draft_fragment" />
    <bpmn:userTask id="review_fragment" name="Review extension">
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <zeebe:userTask />
        <zeebe:formDefinition formId="craft_review_form" />
        <zeebe:ioMapping>
          <zeebe:output source="=approval" target="approval" />
        </zeebe:ioMapping>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>lint_ok</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>to_gw_approve</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:userTask>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="to_gw_approve" sourceRef="review_fragment" targetRef="gw_approve" />
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="gw_approve" name="Approved?" default="rejected">
      <bpmn:incoming>to_gw_approve</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>approved</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>rejected</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="approved" name="apply" sourceRef="gw_approve" targetRef="apply_extension">
      <bpmn:conditionExpression xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">=approval = "apply"</bpmn:conditionExpression>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="rejected" name="reject" sourceRef="gw_approve" targetRef="gw_rejected_entry" />
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="apply_extension" name="Splice into the session graph">
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <zeebe:taskDefinition type="graph:extend" />
        <zeebe:ioMapping>
          <zeebe:input source="=fragment" target="fragment" />
          <zeebe:output source="=status" target="extend_status" />
        </zeebe:ioMapping>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>approved</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>to_applied</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="to_applied" sourceRef="apply_extension" targetRef="craft_applied" />
    <bpmn:endEvent id="craft_applied" name="Extension applied">
      <bpmn:incoming>to_applied</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="craft_rejected" name="Extension rejected">
      <bpmn:incoming>into_craft_rejected</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
  </bpmn:process>
  <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="BPMNDiagram_craft_graph">
    <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="BPMNPlane_craft_graph" bpmnElement="craft_graph">
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="craft_start_di" bpmnElement="craft_start">
        <dc:Bounds x="57" y="52" width="36" height="36" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="gw_draft_entry_di" bpmnElement="gw_draft_entry" isMarkerVisible="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="200" y="45" width="50" height="50" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="draft_fragment_di" bpmnElement="draft_fragment">
        <dc:Bounds x="325" y="30" width="100" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="lint_fragment_di" bpmnElement="lint_fragment">
        <dc:Bounds x="475" y="30" width="100" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="layout_fragment_di" bpmnElement="layout_fragment">
        <dc:Bounds x="625" y="30" width="100" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="gw_lint_di" bpmnElement="gw_lint" isMarkerVisible="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="800" y="45" width="50" height="50" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="review_fragment_di" bpmnElement="review_fragment">
        <dc:Bounds x="925" y="30" width="100" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="gw_approve_di" bpmnElement="gw_approve" isMarkerVisible="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="1100" y="45" width="50" height="50" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="apply_extension_di" bpmnElement="apply_extension">
        <dc:Bounds x="1225" y="30" width="100" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="craft_applied_di" bpmnElement="craft_applied">
        <dc:Bounds x="1407" y="52" width="36" height="36" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="gw_rejected_entry_di" bpmnElement="gw_rejected_entry" isMarkerVisible="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="1550" y="45" width="50" height="50" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="craft_rejected_di" bpmnElement="craft_rejected">
        <dc:Bounds x="1707" y="52" width="36" height="36" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="to_draft_di" bpmnElement="to_draft">
        <di:waypoint x="93" y="70" />
        <di:waypoint x="200" y="70" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="into_draft_fragment_di" bpmnElement="into_draft_fragment">
        <di:waypoint x="250" y="70" />
        <di:waypoint x="325" y="70" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="to_lint_di" bpmnElement="to_lint">
        <di:waypoint x="425" y="70" />
        <di:waypoint x="475" y="70" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="to_layout_di" bpmnElement="to_layout">
        <di:waypoint x="575" y="70" />
        <di:waypoint x="625" y="70" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="to_gw_lint_di" bpmnElement="to_gw_lint">
        <di:waypoint x="725" y="70" />
        <di:waypoint x="800" y="70" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="lint_ok_di" bpmnElement="lint_ok">
        <di:waypoint x="850" y="70" />
        <di:waypoint x="925" y="70" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="lint_exhausted_di" bpmnElement="lint_exhausted">
        <di:waypoint x="825" y="95" />
        <di:waypoint x="825" y="140" />
        <di:waypoint x="1575" y="140" />
        <di:waypoint x="1575" y="95" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="lint_retry_di" bpmnElement="lint_retry">
        <di:waypoint x="825" y="95" />
        <di:waypoint x="825" y="140" />
        <di:waypoint x="375" y="140" />
        <di:waypoint x="375" y="110" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="to_gw_approve_di" bpmnElement="to_gw_approve">
        <di:waypoint x="1025" y="70" />
        <di:waypoint x="1100" y="70" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="approved_di" bpmnElement="approved">
        <di:waypoint x="1150" y="70" />
        <di:waypoint x="1225" y="70" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="rejected_di" bpmnElement="rejected">
        <di:waypoint x="1125" y="95" />
        <di:waypoint x="1125" y="140" />
        <di:waypoint x="1575" y="140" />
        <di:waypoint x="1575" y="95" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="to_applied_di" bpmnElement="to_applied">
        <di:waypoint x="1325" y="70" />
        <di:waypoint x="1407" y="70" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="into_craft_rejected_di" bpmnElement="into_craft_rejected">
        <di:waypoint x="1600" y="70" />
        <di:waypoint x="1707" y="70" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
    </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
  </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
</bpmn:definitions>
